\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces Recovery compresses the cross-support range from 2.675\,pp to 0.118\,pp, far below the $0.52$\,pp per-checkpoint binomial-SE sampling-noise scale (\S  \ref {app:sf-ast-stats}). This is a descriptive marginal-scale comparison; the aggregates do not identify paired or joint uncertainty. The weaker native supports gain most and the ALPS$\leftrightarrow $ProxSparse rank flips.}}{11}{table.5}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:recovery-compression}{{5}{11}{Recovery compresses the cross-support range from 2.675\,pp to 0.118\,pp, far below the $0.52$\,pp per-checkpoint binomial-SE sampling-noise scale (\S \ref {app:sf-ast-stats}). This is a descriptive marginal-scale comparison; the aggregates do not identify paired or joint uncertainty. The weaker native supports gain most and the ALPS$\leftrightarrow $ProxSparse rank flips}{table.5}{}}
